// PBR look-development grid (plan step 6): 5 x 5 spheres, roughness 0.05 -> 1 along +X, metallic 0 -> 1 along +Y,
// one warm key and one cool fill light over a neutral gray floor. inlineMaterial entries use the material
// library format (assets/materials/base/materials.json). The hemispheric ambient is bright, with a darker ground, so
// that metals, which have no diffuse lobe, show their tinted reflection of the sky and of the ground. The background
// radiance is exposed and tonemapped like the scene: #36383A is displayed as #202224. With the default bloom only the
// mirror-like highlights of the glossy spheres glow, faintly and steadily (the Karis average of the bloom bounds what a
// tiny highlight adds, so it does not pulse as the camera moves); the spheres themselves never bloom. No vignette, so
// that the spheres in the corners are judged at the same exposure as the central ones.
